[{:db/id "q-122306/selection/49eb9e36f1f7c170a3bf1b697cdf843dc961eb0ae4e1981964ee41a314119ccc" :answer/id #uuid "0802490b-c4c2-55b2-ab92-28c76b11d624" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{44}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306/selection/2d2215e1fcbdbd3b3c8f9e572c8414e7645b97fbce56e1adc1f860e376c34226" :answer/id #uuid "0feba903-8267-54b7-9df4-15dbc5a8e353" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{13}{22}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306/selection/53f4800d9d2fb52dedd8523646873667ac942dcb1a72f31e84c12c34393adb50" :answer/id #uuid "e918507c-cf03-5757-82fb-222ad862d1b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{44}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306/selection/25022227e6bd58299dbc0c8864e17dd30b4792d7e3fa4a9738a4239f13ff1b56" :answer/id #uuid "7a670870-2343-5277-b441-bde35d4095a8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{44}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306/selection/f9533fd017b819f8a8d2833fa5c17a54e22e5e9275eb2685d8ccd0735247ec95" :answer/id #uuid "fc461954-364c-5ac9-9512-f69d1908ffa5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7}{44}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5f79430e-9462-5ae8-9b51-a3eb667f495c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122306/selection/f9533fd017b819f8a8d2833fa5c17a54e22e5e9275eb2685d8ccd0735247ec95" :answer-field/choices ["q-122306/selection/49eb9e36f1f7c170a3bf1b697cdf843dc961eb0ae4e1981964ee41a314119ccc" "q-122306/selection/2d2215e1fcbdbd3b3c8f9e572c8414e7645b97fbce56e1adc1f860e376c34226" "q-122306/selection/53f4800d9d2fb52dedd8523646873667ac942dcb1a72f31e84c12c34393adb50" "q-122306/selection/25022227e6bd58299dbc0c8864e17dd30b4792d7e3fa4a9738a4239f13ff1b56" "q-122306/selection/f9533fd017b819f8a8d2833fa5c17a54e22e5e9275eb2685d8ccd0735247ec95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122306" :question/id #uuid "6943a89b-51ba-5049-a4c3-036341b2c35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122306" :question/problem "In a class, $20$ students are boys, and $24$ are girls. $5%$ of the boys are engaged in a sports section, and $25%$ of the girls are engaged in a sports section. What is the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section?" :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that the selected student is engaged in a sports section, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap {B}^{′})\n$$\n\nThere are $20$ boys in the class, and $5%$ of them are engaged in a sports section. So, the number of boys engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{100}\\cdot 20=1.\n$$\n\nThere are $24$  girls in the class, and $25%$ of them are engaged in a sports section. So, the number of girls  engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\frac{25}{100}\\cdot 24=6.\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(S\\cap B),$ we take the number of boys engaged in a sports section $(1)$ and divide it by the total number of students in the class $(20+24=44).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap B)=\\frac{1}{44}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(S\\cap {B}^{′}),$ we take the number of girls engaged in a sports section $(6)$ and divide it by the total number of students in the class $(44).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap {B}^{′})=\\frac{6}{44}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student is engaged in a sports section is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap B)+P(S\\cap {B}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{44}+\\frac{6}{44} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{44}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122306/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122306"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "3023f36c-eb25-51ae-a411-c717ad0db959" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" :answer/id #uuid "6fb5b3a4-a852-5123-91fd-6df2bf43bc16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" :answer/id #uuid "ecdb937b-4541-5ad6-8a20-01a03b4b1c0c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" :answer/id #uuid "2e16ff51-48c5-57e3-89a6-9d9d895369b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{4}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "0b50dd2e-223c-5bee-a71e-8e2f3abad80b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b2c9694e-34c6-5f3f-8b2d-d21304c9cc80" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88830/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer-field/choices ["q-88830/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" "q-88830/selection/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" "q-88830/selection/d427b944e26709d5f365fc6b5711be004a0a3509f614cbfd4943dc70d3f6d84e" "q-88830/selection/3089f9a34f7a805d8b2b2d5d51b10dc7aea027e8ec8fd8d06ad11cecf2ba9740" "q-88830/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88830" :question/id #uuid "95918580-9eee-5598-9f0d-4111cb92fbec" :question/math-academy-id "q-88830" :question/problem "In a class, $17$ students are boys, and $23$ are girls. Of the boys, $2$ belong to the school chess club. Of the girls, $3$ are in the chess club. What is the probability that a randomly selected student in the class is in the chess club?" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen student is on the chess club, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student is on the chess club, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C\\cap B)+P(C\\cap {B}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(C\\cap B),$ we take the number of students in the class who are on the chess club and are boys $(2)$ and divide by the total number of students in the class $(17+23=40).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap B)=\\frac{2}{40}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(C\\cap {B}^{′}),$ we take the number of students in the class who are on the chess club and are girls $(3)$ and divide by the total number of students in the class $(40).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap {B}^{′})=\\frac{3}{40}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student is on the chess club is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap B)+P(C\\cap {B}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{40}+\\frac{3}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{40} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88830/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88830"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "a090565b-1a19-5a44-989c-0755c93fd0ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" :answer/id #uuid "64c11af1-38ec-5056-85d3-f7f60287e49f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" :answer/id #uuid "66ac889a-eb70-5b87-9794-de4263c4241f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{4}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer/id #uuid "824b12f8-20c6-5453-a979-a729eaaee723" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903" :answer/id #uuid "2f577ca1-c818-5e5e-a3e2-271bbaa936d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e326adc8-e341-55a0-b4b0-956bab5b1d3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" :answer-field/choices ["q-88922/selection/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-88922/selection/d027d90726f5bdbf1525aade1b6bde5c85e2082f2b792dfacee399fcc90e9833" "q-88922/selection/b93157e0eb36ec8e645eeabaa0819400f448209e0db24c1abf59704822466393" "q-88922/selection/523b37883474afade764165f552bc128b7640323ff7244275508d19e6f99b277" "q-88922/selection/8bb646af439794acfbd313a6a7eb86a2818f1f792118f7583677724bca2d9903"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88922" :question/id #uuid "d0ecdd68-13a0-5025-b2d2-94155866cbce" :question/math-academy-id "q-88922" :question/problem "A gas station offers two types of gasoline, regular and premium. On a certain day, of the $43$ customers who bought regular gas, $23$ paid with a credit card. On the same day, of the $38$ customers that bought premium gas, $31$ of them paid with a credit card. What is the probability of a randomly selected customer paying with a credit card?" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen person paid with a credit card, and let $R$ be the event that the person bought regular gas. Then ${R}^{′}$ is the event that the person bought premium gas.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person paid with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C\\cap R)+P(C\\cap {R}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(C\\cap R),$ we take the number of people who bought regular gas and paid with a credit card $(23)$ and divide by the total number of customers on that day $(43+38=81).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap R)=\\frac{23}{81}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(C\\cap {R}^{′}),$ we take the number of people who bought premium gas and paid with a credit card $(31)$ and divide by the total number of customers on that day $(81).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(C\\cap {R}^{′})=\\frac{31}{81}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person paid with a credit card is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C\\cap R)+P(C\\cap {R}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{23}{81}+\\frac{31}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{54}{81} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88922/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88922"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" :answer/id #uuid "a3c48099-365c-527a-a489-6b77feda06e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" :answer/id #uuid "0f6e5f31-2ef6-5826-b822-30771464fb4b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer/id #uuid "b265767a-d892-530b-a675-91707afd969b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" :answer/id #uuid "bb10ad24-7a0b-5f05-99d2-925d73c1553b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{2}{7}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555" :answer/id #uuid "a7c84331-3f1e-5da2-8c93-026e1f2c4a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{8}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4882a8ae-982e-563f-9966-d6be916e01ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88892/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" :answer-field/choices ["q-88892/selection/d3a7133ef1a1f6526aaec763d522f5ae075d8386a4606de90dcb93094f1d21d6" "q-88892/selection/21bc1f5ac2b6db8ca11973d9b85c1eeb6af2cd920b556e0cf3d98ab9a728286a" "q-88892/selection/9e11fa4df3725c69efaf2fb0a82d90e47a4519d002f721e23606c3d6290fb02c" "q-88892/selection/6aa0658ec3b64327f8a2d599faa4f715c940036c4e92b012fbfb8370208f2e7d" "q-88892/selection/3a3e10526f40c673b7703a3c103fe7589223997acb2a083d0e3a20b742c55555"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88892" :question/id #uuid "4f027c79-6eb0-5320-9fc8-81849b6c264f" :question/math-academy-id "q-88892" :question/problem "Alice has two email accounts, $A$ and $B.$ In account $A,$ she received $24$ emails of which $5$ are spam. In the account $B,$ she received $18$ emails of which $2$ are spam. What is the probability that a randomly selected email in either account is spam?" :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen email is spam, and let $A$ be the event that the email was received in account $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the email was received in account $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap {A}^{′})\n$$\n\nTo calculate $P(S\\cap A),$ we take the number of emails in account A that are spam $(5)$ and divide by the total number of emails received $(24+18=42).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap A)=\\frac{5}{42}.\n$$\n\nSimilarly, to calculate $P(S\\cap {A}^{′}),$ we take the number of emails in account $B$ that are spam $(2)$ and divide by the total number of emails received $(24+18=42).$ So, we have\n\n$$\nP(S\\cap {A}^{′})=\\frac{2}{42}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected email is spam is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S\\cap A)+P(S\\cap {A}^{′}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{42}+\\frac{2}{42} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{42} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-88892/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88892"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122397/selection/514e33c9b858c825c428dba350b8264609585198d932cd8e87f5a118b0dd2847" :answer/id #uuid "ecedb263-cddb-5a5f-b6b4-09b85c85846f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.18" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122397/selection/61c5d15ea0523c8a1f01509199218ed2a7006cabc3a7e335b1d7a4174bb7e981" :answer/id #uuid "9c481742-707b-5237-88