n person is a male, and let $U$ be the event that the chosen person is under $18.$ Then, ${U}^{′}$ is the event that the person is $18$ or over.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person is a male, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(M)=P(M\\cap U)+P(M\\cap {U}^{′})\n$$\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nP(M\\cap U)=0.18,\\,P(M\\cap {U}^{′})=0.54.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected person is a male is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(M) & =P(M\\cap U)+P(M\\cap {U}^{′}) \\\\  & =0.18+0.54 \\\\  & =0.72.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-122397/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c07eb336-1ac8-5633-abaf-fcfca4c12bd1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122397"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3" :answer/id #uuid "ab3c0f67-fddf-55d9-bd45-dd88f4b249b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" :answer/id #uuid "c3c9143e-4f71-563d-b094-54ce9bb65b7f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{9}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection/63560ca0ca7d09733261935dc2bd0c9c7c25e5c2ee469d189671be7ed67bf209" :answer/id #uuid "28f8e32b-32c6-585a-bd63-ddbc1bea88ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{11}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection/df99d56d846c0bfd62e2553820ccb4af8b1a2a04a683f77fcd4158037e51e762" :answer/id #uuid "b15ea9f0-6569-556b-bff3-708a2d847938" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{9}{50}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection/a1295f2061c7c4ce210cd459bc8112b9a94f194ef869710e6409a0dcaf9a6b57" :answer/id #uuid "80e8e961-53e9-5144-b814-84be4d81580b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{100}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "74879bd6-5325-5128-a562-4a6802ea22ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89031/selection/df99d56d846c0bfd62e2553820ccb4af8b1a2a04a683f77fcd4158037e51e762" :answer-field/choices ["q-89031/selection/0064d374f806cba8ea43a11831d2980495c6733de7e909ec06431bd236f4f2b3" "q-89031/selection/e3b46c3e63ee8ef5a071cd8ef5f7250114c0c6983477af061861d82a06039d46" "q-89031/selection/63560ca0ca7d09733261935dc2bd0c9c7c25e5c2ee469d189671be7ed67bf209" "q-89031/selection/df99d56d846c0bfd62e2553820ccb4af8b1a2a04a683f77fcd4158037e51e762" "q-89031/selection/a1295f2061c7c4ce210cd459bc8112b9a94f194ef869710e6409a0dcaf9a6b57"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89031" :question/id #uuid "408466b2-d5d7-5a6f-92f2-2e2d6c4b81d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-89031" :question/problem "A certain disease is present in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the population. A test to detect the disease gives a positive result in $\\frac{9}{10}$ of the people with the disease and in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the people without the disease. What is the probability that a randomly selected patient tests positive for the disease?" :question/worked-solution "Let $A$ be the event that the test is positive for the selected patient, and let $D$ be the event that the patient has the disease. Then, ${D}^{′}$ is the event that the patient does not have the disease.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected patient gives a positive result, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(A)=P(A|D)P(D)+P(A|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the disease is present in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the population, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=\\frac{1}{10},\\,P({D}^{′})=\\frac{9}{10}.\n$$\n\n- Since the test gives a positive result in $\\frac{9}{10}$ of the people with the disease, and in $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the people without the disease, we have\n\n$$\nP(A|D)=\\frac{9}{10},\\,P(A|{D}^{′})=\\frac{1}{10}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected patient tests positive for the disease is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(A) & =P(A|D)P(D)+P(A|{D}^{′})P({D}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{9}{10})(\\frac{1}{10})+(\\frac{1}{10})(\\frac{9}{10}) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{100}+\\frac{9}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{18}{100} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{50}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89031/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89031"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88980"] :question/problem "Sophia has two email accounts, account $A$ and account $B.$ She receives $35%$ of her emails in account $A,$ and the remaining $65%$ go into account $B.$ Approximately $15%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam while $25%$ of the emails received in account $B$ are spam. What is the probability that a randomly selected email is spam?" :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen email is spam, and let $A$ be the event that the email selected is from account $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the email selected is from account $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected email is spam, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $35%$ of the emails are received in account $A$ and the remaining $65%$ in account $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.35,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.65.\n$$\n\n- Since $15%$ of the emails received in account $A$ are spam while $25%$ of the emails received in account $B$ are spam, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|A)=0.15,\\,P(S|{A}^{′})=0.25.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected email is spam is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|A)P(A)+P(S|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.15)(0.35)+(0.25)(0.65) \\\\  & =0.215.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection/d38061c1c53688567301cba5c58591e5bfd7f4f0c062ba3a3079edf40865036c" :answer/id #uuid "6d4b2075-eb10-5e2e-a960-abbdce3f9921" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.312" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection/4dc78589657cba1307b33bb2cda5228b998e97b2e222408cd7c8944b9207e1c0" :answer/id #uuid "87ab7379-f694-5997-b5bb-f6d10fe3535e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.213" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection/3d442cffd13050216e5bbf16cf8738897a00ae015613cf785b8d81e95824820b" :answer/id #uuid "8642fbe2-99a1-5834-97ce-6dcc27e3977a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.227" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection/08da2abbdc7b4530519abeca6487ec34da284a62a989a5f1af3d42f5171b5d2f" :answer/id #uuid "961152f7-bee5-558f-bce0-6ef9f0c80ef7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.207" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection/39a2f9b3fa29bb7e47f11b448868a795e88ec13d4fcf51093756a5ede16cbd4c" :answer/id #uuid "be3c9adf-bc12-52f3-a569-7a970a8a76bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.197" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "fdf28614-efc7-52f0-bd6a-d1efea9c55ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89041/selection/08da2abbdc7b4530519abeca6487ec34da284a62a989a5f1af3d42f5171b5d2f" :answer-field/choices ["q-89041/selection/d38061c1c53688567301cba5c58591e5bfd7f4f0c062ba3a3079edf40865036c" "q-89041/selection/4dc78589657cba1307b33bb2cda5228b998e97b2e222408cd7c8944b9207e1c0" "q-89041/selection/3d442cffd13050216e5bbf16cf8738897a00ae015613cf785b8d81e95824820b" "q-89041/selection/08da2abbdc7b4530519abeca6487ec34da284a62a989a5f1af3d42f5171b5d2f" "q-89041/selection/39a2f9b3fa29bb7e47f11b448868a795e88ec13d4fcf51093756a5ede16cbd4c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89041" :question/id #uuid "846490bd-6254-5a08-8e31-cc536ddf844b" :question/math-academy-id "q-89041" :question/problem "A math teacher split their calculus class into two groups, Group $A$ and Group $B.$ Group $A$ has $43%$ of the total number of students, while Group $B$ has $57%$ of the total number of students. If $23%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, and $19%$ of the students in Group $B$ obtained the top grade, what is the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade?" :question/worked-solution "Let $G$ be the event that the chosen student obtained the top grade, and let $A$ be the event that the student is from Group $A.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the student is from Group $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student obtained the top grade, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(G)=P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $43%$ of their students are in Group $A$ and $57%$ are in Group $B$, we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.43,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.57.\n$$\n\n- Since $23%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade and $19%$ of the students in Group $B$ obtained the top grade, we have\n\n$$\nP(G|A)=0.23,\\,P(G|{A}^{′})=0.19.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G) & =P(G|A)P(A)+P(G|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\  & =(0.23)(0.43)+(0.19)(0.57) \\\\  & ≈0.207\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-89041/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89041"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-88578"] :question/problem "In a class, $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the students are boys, and $\\frac{2}{3}$ are girls. Of the boys, $\\frac{1}{6}$ of them play soccer, and of the girls, $\\frac{1}{4}$ of them play soccer. What is the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer?" :question/worked-solution "Let $S$ be the event that the chosen student plays soccer, and let $B$ be the event that the student is a boy. Then ${B}^{′}$ is the event that the student is a girl.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(S)=P(S|B)P(B)+P(S|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the students are boys and $\\frac{2}{3}$ are girls, we have\n\n$$\nP(B)=\\frac{1}{3},\\,P({B}^{′})=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\n- Since $\\frac{1}{6}$ of the boys play soccer and $\\frac{1}{4}$ of the girls play soccer, we have\n\n$$\nP(S|B)=\\frac{1}{6},\\,P(S|{B}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected student plays soccer is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(S) & =P(S|B)P(B)+P(S|{B}^{′})P({B}^{′}) \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{6})(\\frac{1}{3})+(\\frac{1}{4})(\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{18}+\\frac{1}{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1+3}{18} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" :answer/id #uuid "01a29caa-0474-5e8d-a7cf-07a5a46279dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "a2556848-ff90-5916-b237-9f6036542386" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection/5c50c1056e48f42de075a91a2f74cc01eba98b95841066d5a7cef518aa641cc6" :answer/id #uuid "a5eecca0-4a81-5159-9815-0a0e4c3552cd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.68" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection/61c5d15ea0523c8a1f01509199218ed2a7006cabc3a7e335b1d7a4174bb7e981" :answer/id #uuid "03d3e4c7-7e88-5d61-91aa-54699b28a5ce" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.72" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "5bff7b5d-fde0-5ef4-a262-9b2f058cc694" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d84c8f8-d6ad-56c7-881d-b4732341da43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-88977/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" :answer-field/choices ["q-88977/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" "q-88977/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-88977/selection/5c50c1056e48f42de075a91a2f74cc01eba98b95841066d5a7cef518aa641cc6" "q-88977/selection/61c5d15ea0523c8a1f01509199218ed2a7006cabc3a7e335b1d7a4174bb7e981" "q-88977/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-88977" :question/id #uuid "4e8c8220-3427-51b3-8588-a7be73c3dc45" :question/math-academy-id "q-88977" :question/problem "A student answers a multiple-choice test. Each question of the test has four possible answers, and only one choice is correct. The student knows the correct answer for $60%$ of the questions. If the student decides to select an answer at random for the questions that she does not know the answer to, what is the probability that a randomly selected question on the test is correct?" :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the selected question is correct, and let $K$ be the event that the student knew the answer. Then ${K}^{′}$ is the event that the student did not know the answer.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected question is correct, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since the student knows the answer to $60%$ of the questions, we have\n\n$$\nP(K)=0.6,\\,P({K}^{′})=0.4.\n$$\n\n- Since each question has four possible answers, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|K)=1,\\,P(C|{K}^{′})=\\frac{1}{4}=0.25.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability, the probability that a randomly selected question on the test is correct is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|K)P(K)+P(C|{K}^{′})P({K}^{′}) \\\\  & =(1)(0.6)+(0.25)(0.4) \\\\  & =0.6+0.1 \\\\  & =0.70.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-88977/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "f0f7055d-9f45-5115-97f4-35d0c56008e0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-88977"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection/250d79f96fe0538363a39ff6475c3291963c6a55bc727ce128daeb62e061a964" :answer/id #uuid "70dd2be3-17ea-5aa0-998e-febe1f3b4c52" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.05" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection/e733dc6bf0b88b1c1b230e32a5cfd5a69828f772e015dc33bed1ec14c8bbe147" :answer/id #uuid "a41b2f5c-cbff-5d4d-bd01-09c4135a062f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.23" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779" :answer/id #uuid "94590f98-8712-5a8e-a21d-76ed66d3694c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" :answer/id #uuid "4631437a-9b6b-5e0d-9d15-50b03bcfd0d2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" :answer/id #uuid "02e76174-bd01-533b-b73f-5c9e5c5849f7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "321bd09c-e3d3-5497-9946-e7eda90a95f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122412/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" :answer-field/choices ["q-122412/selection/250d79f96fe0538363a39ff6475c3291963c6a55bc727ce128daeb62e061a964" "q-122412/selection/e733dc6bf0b88b1c1b230e32a5cfd5a69828f772e015dc33bed1ec14c8bbe147" "q-122412/selection/5846909f174da1ed620d151ac05204e83972966f779efb8f143352f971a29779" "q-122412/selection/57f1df4deeb63ac8b169c1392105cc1ec886c4a882da47e1d3a4a61ab32f1e2a" "q-122412/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122412" :question/id #uuid "d44f26f0-f74d-5614-a0df-014aa1f39a6b" :question/math-academy-id "q-122412" :question/problem "Company $A$ supplies $80%$ of widgets for a car shop and only $1%$ of their widgets turn out to be defective. Company $B$ supplies the remaining $20%$ of widgets. The probability that a widget from the car shop will be defective is $0.014.$ If a customer randomly purchases a widget supplied by company $B,$ what is the probability that it will be defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a widget will be defective, and let $A$ be the event that the widget is supplied by company $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the widget is supplied by company $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly purchased widget will be defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since company $A$ supplies $80%$ of widgets for a car shop and company $B$ the remaining $20%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.80,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.20.\n$$\n\n- Since $1%$ of the widget supplied by company $A$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.01.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a widget from the car shop is defective will be $0.014,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.014.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.014 & =(0.01)(0.80)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.20) \\\\ 0.014 & =0.008+0.20P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.20P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.006 \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected widget supplied by company $B$ will be defective is $0.03.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122412/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122412"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" :answer/id #uuid "3c6ae10f-41b2-5de1-abe1-40985dad7c6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.70" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection/1d3a087895598d91cf464cc7997cc46dbaeabf99b616c1f7780ec32d815a8b02" :answer/id #uuid "0436c47e-08d5-5b11-a423-5e72c7ed4d42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.80" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" :answer/id #uuid "12a2598b-b029-5a5c-a9dd-b8d78497567d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.75" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" :answer/id #uuid "156cfc01-9456-56a6-9143-c47d3248a744" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.65" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe" :answer/id #uuid "3c9ac833-3359-5a89-8200-baf67ed28b0d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.60" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f522b0f2-f7d7-56bf-aee8-db36961299fc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89053/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" :answer-field/choices ["q-89053/selection/5b36c4b70758cba9f6fa0476faab4ecca020a862e5baaac6831d5712f6550044" "q-89053/selection/1d3a087895598d91cf464cc7997cc46dbaeabf99b616c1f7780ec32d815a8b02" "q-89053/selection/bc99aa5f3ee62c40cb834b274ce88683dbffd8fee8404db2b536df0189aa9cdc" "q-89053/selection/a44ed9268297050614edc4097a04d3089044bc70b376ad604b0445193a602b0a" "q-89053/selection/2d1f2a87afc1e31bef511d128d2b8cb63b1f3551be752c982f1c0f205ef816fe"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89053" :question/id #uuid "9f71c3d4-298d-5849-a475-518d54df8b50" :question/math-academy-id "q-89053" :question/problem "In a gas station, $55%$ of the customers buy regular gasoline while $45%$ buy premium gasoline. If $60%$ of the customers that buy regular gasoline usually pay with a credit card and the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $0.645,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected customer who buys premium gasoline usually pays with a credit card? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $C$ be the event that the chosen person pays with a credit card, and let $R$ be the event that the person buys regular gas. Then ${R}^{′}$ is the event that the person buys premium gas.\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected person pays with a credit card, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(C)=P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since $55%$ of the customers buy regular gasoline while $45%$ buy premium gasoline, we have\n\n$$\nP(R)=0.55,\\,P({R}^{′})=0.45.\n$$\n\n- Since $60%$ of the customers that buy regular gasoline pay with a credit card, we have\n\n$$\nP(C|R)=0.60.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected customer pays with a credit card is $0.645,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(C)=0.645.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(C|{R}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(C) & =P(C|R)P(R)+P(C|{R}^{′})P({R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.645 & =(0.60)(0.55)+P(C|{R}^{′})(0.45) \\\\ 0.645 & =0.33+0.45P(C|{R}^{′}) \\\\ 0.45P(C|{R}^{′}) & =0.315 \\\\ P(C|{R}^{′}) & =0.70.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected customer who buys premium gasoline usually pays with a credit card is $0.70.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89053/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89053"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" :answer/id #uuid "c26868d0-20af-533e-acc3-1b08c868e97f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection/28aab08e0495d28a59636ff7f409d8e53451cc8230d6f374a1866d31ffb8df60" :answer/id #uuid "2fa45848-efd9-5d23-a679-2315501d86c7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.17" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" :answer/id #uuid "8b4e8b2e-23f0-51fa-8bbd-c91a4a75ba9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection/dbbd2ab186e6446437720ddefa77970e71256eaf21337e33e8b16e90376bea90" :answer/id #uuid "990519d1-feee-5178-9796-c20ad96631c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7" :answer/id #uuid "cd38b16a-8193-5ee8-a86e-07cbc5bed587" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.20" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "29a91ee7-75c1-5c81-9b3e-691604156c90" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-89042/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" :answer-field/choices ["q-89042/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" "q-89042/selection/28aab08e0495d28a59636ff7f409d8e53451cc8230d6f374a1866d31ffb8df60" "q-89042/selection/5d227958e8e2ab9feb7a492bded665cf59dfa9121f7d82334971c99adf799e26" "q-89042/selection/dbbd2ab186e6446437720ddefa77970e71256eaf21337e33e8b16e90376bea90" "q-89042/selection/ad0364dcc99d42229f6e2a60f5334f760d018ec942404cf40f77f1ced1d561c7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-89042" :question/id #uuid "b38f87cd-849d-519c-9592-01abf17dbe8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-89042" :question/problem "A company manufactures electronic components. Of the total components manufactured, $60%$ of them are produced by machine $A,$ and the remaining $40%$ are produced by machine $B.$ Of the components produced by machine $A,$ $10%$ are defective. In total, $12%$ of all components produced are defective. If a component produced by machine $B$ is selected at random, what is the probability of it being defective? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that the selected component is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the component was produced by machine $A.$ Then ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the component was produced by machine $B.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected component is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine $A$ produces $60%$ of the components and $B$ the remaining $40%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.60,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.40.\n$$\n\n- Since $10%$ of the components produced by machine $A$ are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.10.\n$$\n\n- Since $12%$ of the components produced are defective, we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.12.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.12 & =(0.10)(0.60)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.40) \\\\ 0.12 & =0.06+0.40P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.40P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.06 \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected component produced by machine $B$ is defective is $0.15.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-89042/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-89042"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" :answer/id #uuid "96902438-963c-5218-adf7-cd6a7a46e7f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection/a2d0265579b22da5960607bc1640b7a0be8b50d1be60dc6e9dd834797cda468c" :answer/id #uuid "6536a8d6-bc51-54f9-a0d4-baadba843bcd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" :answer/id #uuid "6906ee86-bfa3-5739-9c54-667b86c46fd0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.03" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection/282a60ed35945ab856866387202a1be5e70a48ce60fad187f57629662d95cbbc" :answer/id #uuid "378b1b33-8e5c-5342-85bc-76e07be00442" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.08" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c" :answer/id #uuid "b2d45c5a-ae2b-50e8-906d-666f6b1282f2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7b9ef9dc-7a01-5439-9c40-638f91b5375c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-122403/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" :answer-field/choices ["q-122403/selection/625896633137e0044aec1ec040d8233380e151c0f7ffbedd051e7544cbdce1c4" "q-122403/selection/a2d0265579b22da5960607bc1640b7a0be8b50d1be60dc6e9dd834797cda468c" "q-122403/selection/91afb9a0ba928957f30252e15bfbaf7fa3834bb4fbb0b0864156247fdeeccc36" "q-122403/selection/282a60ed35945ab856866387202a1be5e70a48ce60fad187f57629662d95cbbc" "q-122403/selection/95a1d5fa369c4d08bda10228102d0fbae8f93732afc4c2ec3773c4f3d47df28c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-122403" :question/id #uuid "aa6ce446-8372-563e-b2d4-b6a175008dba" :question/math-academy-id "q-122403" :question/problem "Two machines ${M}_{1}$ and ${M}_{2}$ in a particular factory produce $75%$ and $25%,$ respectively, of the total daily output of electronic tubes. It is known that $4%$ of the tubes produced by ${M}_{1}$ are defective and that the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective is $0.0375.$ What is the probability that a randomly selected tube produced by ${M}_{2}$ is defective?" :question/worked-solution "Let $D$ be the event that a randomly selected tube is defective, and let $A$ be the event that the tube is produced by machine ${M}_{1}.$ Then, ${A}^{′}$ is the event that the tube is produced by machine ${M}_{2}.$\n\nTo calculate the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective, we can use the law of total probability:\n\n$$\nP(D)=P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′})\n$$\n\nLet's go through the problem statement and translate each bit of information into mathematical notation.\n\n- Since machine ${M}_{1}$ produces $75%$ of the total daily output of electronic tubes and ${M}_{2}$ the remaining $25%,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(A)=0.75,\\,P({A}^{′})=0.25.\n$$\n\n- Since $4%$ of the tubes produced by machine ${M}_{1}$ are defective,  we have\n\n$$\nP(D|A)=0.04.\n$$\n\n- Since the probability that a randomly selected tube from a day's production is defective is $0.0375,$ we have\n\n$$\nP(D)=0.0375.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above information into the law of total probability and solving for $P(D|{A}^{′}),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(D) & =P(D|A)P(A)+P(D|{A}^{′})P({A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.0375 & =(0.04)(0.75)+P(D|{A}^{′})(0.25) \\\\ 0.0375 & =0.03+0.25P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ 0.0075 & =0.25P(D|{A}^{′}) \\\\ P(D|{A}^{′}) & =0.03.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the probability that a randomly selected tube produced by ${M}_{2}$ is defective is $0.03.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-122403/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5000a4b1-c0cb-59f3-9d45-6287fa8ac9b6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-122403"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-89054"] :question/problem "A math teacher splits her calculus class into two groups, Group $A$ and Group $B.$ Of the total students, $35%$ of her students are in Group $A,$ and $65%$ are in Group $B.$ If $20%$ of the students in Group $A$ obtained the top grade, and the probability that a randomly selected student from either group obtained the top grade is $0.265,$ what is the probability that a randomly selected student from Group $B$ obtained the top grade? Round your answer to $2$ decimal places." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-7863"] :question/problem "In box ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/94276c7f8de725803347541a3a00e124915f54c89e0908f256f903f32e990c73.png) there are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/26eecbf5965af5ad8a5a3ef715bb6e0fa969d36ffafbccaccea2a19616b25eb2.png) marbles, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/a1aa710a9396fec0487bfd728e836f7188caa9a03b1d66d79d88948ba32e32ca.png) of which are green. In box ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/762b6cc7cc4d4c8fc3553d61e1779ae5e08597476c0101011b9d3824730e88ed.png) there are ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/cc635e1b92c71b63fbb85b82a6e5057ccec707d58b8a3a8c64d558004d1a26d1.png) marbles, ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071098/assets/4f94b41c8502c080528c0ca826a6a02aa2e60acba9b8506c41cfb9629e2a2077.png) of which are green. The marbles from the two boxes are mixed, and one marble is randomly chosen from the mixture. What is the probability that the selected marble is green?" :question/worked-solution "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Aca